 "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I booked Dana Lee's flight and hotel, and both are confirmed. They're two separate reservations instead of one combined trip.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, nonstop, $289. This is the cheapest nonstop. The one-stop F120 is cheaper at $199, but it has a stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge (H1), New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This is the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1000 limit, so no manager approval was needed.\n\n**What happened:** I tried to book both together with `book_trip`, but the request timed out. I retried it with the same request key, which can't charge twice, and the system said the first attempt had partly failed: the flight was booked but the hotel step hit an internal error. Then I booked the hotel by itself. Dana's reservation list now shows exactly one flight and one hotel, with no duplicate charges.", "type": "text"}]}]}